ufficient thymine intake as  a result they become thymine deficient  thereby causing brain cells to die  here's a heartbreaking example of  wernicke korsakoff syndrome in a  middle-aged man this affects a lot of  people's lives  two years ago  my brother don had been found on his  floor  unresponsive  he had laid there for at least five days  because there was five newspapers on his  porch he had drank  so much that  he ended up  with something is called warnickies  i think some people caught wet brain  which i've never heard of it before this  happened  and  he was in the hospital  for about two weeks and he was in  mcmurray hills  manor nursing home  and then the nursing home said that  there was nothing else they could do for  him and they wanted him to leave there  so  not realizing how hard this was going to  be i brought him home with me his  current condition  is um  he uh he has dementia  and he has  no memory even his longtime memory  he remembers little bits of things but a  lot of things like i've showed him a  couple places where we lived and he  doesn't remember  and it's hard because  like i had said before  you you lose yourself you you know you  lose yourself in this like it  everything is him  next onto the digestive system if the  alcohol you're drinking is more than 15  alcohol by volume it can delay digestion  of food in the stomach and intestines  concentrations at 15 or higher denatures  digestive enzymes needed to break down  food as a result bacteria in your gut  digest the food for you and release  their own gaseous byproducts causing  abdominal discomfort among other things  at the intestines alcohol is absorbed  into the blood it's true that some  alcohol does get absorbed through the  stomach but most is through the  intestines all the alcohol you drank is  now in your blood and gets sent  throughout your body some alcohol does  pass through your lungs and because  ethanol has a low molecular weight and  is quite volatile it gets exhaled 